## Implementation: Swap pdf-parse for @llamaindex/liteparse

### Changes Made

1. **lib/generation/extract.ts** — Rewrote `extractPdf()`:
   - Removed `pdfjs-dist` text extraction (server-side); kept `pdfjs-dist` as dep for client PDF viewer
   - Added `@llamaindex/liteparse` for bounding-box-aware text extraction via PDFium
   - Phase 1: non-OCR parse → get TextItem[] with x/y/width/height per item
   - Phase 2: detect scanned pages (text coverage < 2% + < 5 items) → selective OCR re-parse
   - Phase 3: group items into lines (y-proximity threshold: avgHeight × 0.3) then paragraphs (y-gap > medianHeight × 0.6) — preserving same ChunkBBox format for react-pdf-highlighter
   - Phase 4: screenshot image-sparse pages (< 150 chars text) via liteparse.screenshot(), apply findFocusedCropBounds, save PNG

2. **package.json** — Removed `pdf-parse` (unused) + `@types/pdf-parse`; added `@llamaindex/liteparse ^2.0.4`

3. **lib/generation/extract.test.ts** — New test file covering:
   - `stripFences()` utility
   - Plain-text extraction and chunk splitting
   - Code-file extraction
   - Image-file extraction

